; A node naming a type the registry beside it does not declare. It is canonical,
; so `dfcad fmt --check` passes over it, and it is what makes `dfcad check`
; refuse the model outright rather than report a rule which did not hold.
;
; That refusal has no machine form to annotate from — the load diagnostic is
; carried by the commands which report per file, and check reports per rule — so
; the gate says so in an annotation of its own and the log carries the file, the
; line and the caret.
(node
  site:S-002
  (label "Meeting Room B")
  (kind Space)
  (type BroomCupboard)
  (geometry area)
  (frame frame:building))
